WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.549
That night after dinner, Mom washed the dishes and Joy dried them.

2
00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:09.365
"My report will be about building friendships.

3
00:00:09.366 --> 00:00:17.149
I’ve already read my section of the book and looked up the topic on the Internet," Joy explained to her family.

4
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.539
"Katie’s topic is exercise."

5
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.481
Katie was looking at her Be Healthy! book.

6
00:00:23.482 --> 00:00:26.199
"I haven’t read my section yet.

7
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.455
But I already know why exercise is good for us.

8
00:00:30.456 --> 00:00:38.099
I just have to use my imagination, like Ms. Barrow said, to make my report interesting and fun."

9
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:43.177
"You should get the whole class to exercise together," said Joy.

10
00:00:43.178 --> 00:00:46.417
"That’s a good idea," said Dad.

11
00:00:46.418 --> 00:00:50.182
"What kind of exercise?" asked Katie.

12
00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:56.409
"Jumping jacks?" Joy sprang back from the sink and began doing jumping jacks.

13
00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.015
Mom grabbed a mug from her hand.

14
00:00:59.016 --> 00:01:01.755
"Don’t break the dishes!"

15
00:01:01.756 --> 00:01:06.091
"That definitely won’t work for my report," said Katie.

16
00:01:06.092 --> 00:01:08.424
"What about you, Grandpa?

17
00:01:08.425 --> 00:01:14.221
"I get my exercise when I work in the garden and clean the house," said Grandpa.

18
00:01:14.222 --> 00:01:18.671
"If kids just did their chores, they’d be healthy enough."

19
00:01:18.672 --> 00:01:22.620
"Be serious, Grandpa," said Katie.

20
00:01:22.621 --> 00:01:24.869
"I am serious!"

21
00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.567
"Dad?" said Katie.

22
00:01:27.568 --> 00:01:31.861
"You kids could run a race," Dad suggested.

23
00:01:31.862 --> 00:01:35.057
"How about dancing?" said Joy.

24
00:01:35.058 --> 00:01:38.654
"The polka!" said Grandpa.

25
00:01:38.655 --> 00:01:43.132
He grabbed Joy, and they went flying around the kitchen.

26
00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:48.462
"I’m getting dizzy, Grandpa!" Joy laughed.

27
00:01:48.463 --> 00:01:51.663
"How about square dancing?" said Dad.

28
00:01:51.664 --> 00:01:54.950
"Swing your partner!" he called.

29
00:01:54.951 --> 00:02:00.030
He hooked his elbow through Joy’s and swung her around in a circle.

30
00:02:00.031 --> 00:02:06.008
"I think we have some square-dancing music at the library," said Mom.

31
00:02:06.009 --> 00:02:10.817
"This might be kind of fun—and funny!" said Katie.

32
00:02:10.818 --> 00:02:13.523
She thought for a moment.

33
00:02:13.524 --> 00:02:16.179
"I’ll have to show the steps to the class.

34
00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.180
Will you help, Joy?"

35
00:02:18.181 --> 00:02:20.200
"Sure!"

36
00:02:20.201 --> 00:02:23.072
"And tomorrow I’ll ask Carlos and Luke . . ."

37
00:02:23.073 --> 00:02:28.039
Katie groaned and slapped her forehead.

38
00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.377
"Rats! I almost forgot!

39
00:02:30.378 --> 00:02:32.550
I’m mad at Luke."

40
00:02:32.551 --> 00:02:36.249
"You’ll have to forgive him," said Joy.

41
00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:40.430
The next morning, Joy spotted Luke and Carlos.

42
00:02:40.431 --> 00:02:45.247
"They’re talking to Olivia as usual," muttered Katie.

43
00:02:45.248 --> 00:02:47.558
Olivia turned toward the twins.

44
00:02:47.559 --> 00:02:50.542
"I brought you a present," she said.

45
00:02:50.543 --> 00:02:52.728
"An ‘ALOHA’ pencil from Hawaii."

46
00:02:52.729 --> 00:02:57.167
She handed Katie and Joy each a bright pink pencil.

47
00:02:57.168 --> 00:02:59.791
"Thanks!" said Joy.

48
00:02:59.792 --> 00:03:01.891
Katie thanked her too.

49
00:03:01.892 --> 00:03:05.826
"Guess what ‘aloha’ means," said Carlos.

50
00:03:05.827 --> 00:03:09.409
"It means hello, right?" said Joy.

51
00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:14.124
"Yep," said Olivia. "But it also means good-bye!"

52
00:03:14.125 --> 00:03:17.918
"That’s weird," Katie couldn’t help saying.

53
00:03:17.919 --> 00:03:19.399
Luke looked at her.

54
00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.843
"Are you still mad at me?" he asked.

55
00:03:22.844 --> 00:03:31.357
"No," said Katie. "In fact, I’m even going to let you help with my exercise report. Interested?"

56
00:03:31.358 --> 00:03:33.355
"Sure," said Luke.

57
00:03:33.356 --> 00:03:38.434
"If you’re looking for guys who are good at sports, you’ve come to the right place."

58
00:03:38.435 --> 00:03:42.022
"What about you, Carlos?" said Katie.

59
00:03:42.023 --> 00:03:46.462
"Yeah, I’ll help." Carlos bent his arm and felt his muscle.

60
00:03:46.463 --> 00:03:51.552
"We could do some push-ups."

61
00:03:51.553 --> 00:03:55.767
"No, I decided against push-ups," said Katie.

62
00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:58.952
"I need your help with square dancing."

63
00:03:58.953 --> 00:04:03.283
"SQUARE DANCING!" roared Luke and Carlos.

64
00:04:03.284 --> 00:04:07.314
"No way!" said Carlos.

65
00:04:07.315 --> 00:04:13.436
"No square dancing!" said Luke. "No dancing of any kind!"

66
00:04:13.437 --> 00:04:17.219
"Sorry. It’s too late to back out," said Katie.

67
00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.762
"You already agreed."

68
00:04:19.763 --> 00:04:24.528
"But we don’t know how to square-dance, do we, Luke?"

69
00:04:24.529 --> 00:04:26.806
"No problem," said Katie.

70
00:04:26.807 --> 00:04:30.331
"We’re going to practice at my house on Saturday."

71
00:04:30.332 --> 00:04:33.459
"That sounds like fun!" said Olivia.

72
00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:39.461
Katie blinked. "Does Olivia think I’m including her too?" she wondered.

73
00:04:39.462 --> 00:04:44.512
"Er . . . I only need four people," she said quickly.

74
00:04:44.513 --> 00:04:49.198
"Two boys and two girls—Luke, Carlos, Joy, and me.

75
00:04:49.199 --> 00:04:52.675
We’ll teach the steps to the rest of the class."

76
00:04:52.676 --> 00:04:56.908
"Oh," said Olivia, looking down.

77
00:04:56.909 --> 00:04:58.737
Joy looked down too.

78
00:04:58.738 --> 00:05:02.069
She wanted to invite Olivia, but she knew she couldn’t.

79
00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.615
It was Katie’s project.

80
00:05:04.616 --> 00:05:06.784
Katie turned back to the others.

81
00:05:06.785 --> 00:05:10.760
"So we’re all set," she said.

82
00:05:10.761 --> 00:05:14.363
"Don’t forget—Saturday afternoon at one o’clock.

83
00:05:14.364 --> 00:05:20.533
And don’t forget your cowboy hats! HA!"

